IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`
IMPORT `sgg-cessation`

-- Tests for sgg-cessation.l4 (ss 377 to 377D). Expected values are written from the text of each subsection, beside the assertion.
-- Dates: Date day month year. A `-- EXPECT` comment above a #TRACE says what the trace must print; the lead checks each against the output.

§ `Section 377(1): notice that the foreign company has ceased`

-- Arguments: ceased to have a place of business in Singapore; ceased to carry on business in Singapore. Either one starts the duty.
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge with the Registrar notice that it has ceased` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge with the Registrar notice that it has ceased` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge with the Registrar notice that it has ceased` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge with the Registrar notice that it has ceased` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "within 7 days after so ceasing": ceased 1 March 2026, so the seventh day is 8 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the notice was lodged within 7 days after the foreign company ceased` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 8 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the notice was lodged within 7 days after the foreign company ceased` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the notice was lodged within 7 days after the foreign company ceased` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1) the notice was lodged within 7 days after the foreign company ceased` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- the duty with its time limit: lodged on the seventh day it is fulfilled; on the eighth, or never, it is breached.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge the notice within 7 days after it ceases` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 377(1) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore` AT 7
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge the notice within 7 days after it ceases` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 377(1) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore` AT 8
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge the notice within 7 days after it ceases` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)

§ `Section 377(1A): the obligation to lodge documents ceases`

-- Arguments: the notice was lodged; the day it was lodged; the document ought to have been lodged before that day; the day asked.
#ASSERT `s 377(1A) the obligation of the foreign company to lodge the document with the Registrar has ceased` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1A) the obligation of the foreign company to lodge the document with the Registrar has ceased` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Starting on the day on which the foreign company lodged the notice": the day before, the obligation has not ceased.
#ASSERT `s 377(1A) the obligation of the foreign company to lodge the document with the Registrar has ceased` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(not being a document that ought to have been lodged before that day)".
#ASSERT `s 377(1A) the obligation of the foreign company to lodge the document with the Registrar has ceased` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(1A) the obligation of the foreign company to lodge the document with the Registrar has ceased` FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 377(1B): the Registrar records the cessation`

-- Arguments: the notice mentioned in subsection (1) was lodged; the case that applies ("as the case may be").
#ASSERT `s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 377(2): liquidation or dissolution`

-- Arguments: the company has gone into liquidation; it has been dissolved in its place of incorporation or origin; the person was an authorised representative immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings.
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the liquidation or the dissolution` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the liquidation or the dissolution` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the liquidation or the dissolution` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the liquidation or the dissolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: the day the liquidation or the dissolution commenced; the day the notice was lodged; the Registrar in special circumstances allowed further time; the last day of that further time.
-- Commenced 1 June 2026: the fourteenth day is 15 June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the notice was lodged within the time the subsection allows` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the notice was lodged within the time the subsection allows` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 16 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) "within such further time as the Registrar in special circumstances allows".
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the notice was lodged within the time the subsection allows` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 16 6 2026) TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the notice was lodged within the time the subsection allows` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the notice was lodged within the time the subsection allows` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a further time the Registrar did not allow is no further time.
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the notice was lodged within the time the subsection allows` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 16 6 2026) FALSE (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: the company has gone into liquidation; a liquidator has been appointed; the person was an authorised representative immediately before the commencement.
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (a) 14 days after the commencement.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 377(2)(a) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within 14 days` "Raj Nair" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` "Raj Nair" DOES `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has gone into liquidation or has been dissolved` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 377(2)(a) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within 14 days` "Raj Nair" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` "Raj Nair" DOES `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has gone into liquidation or has been dissolved` AT 15
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 377(2)(a) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within 14 days` "Raj Nair" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- (b) the further time the Registrar allows: 30 days from the commencement.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 377(2)(b) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within the further time the Registrar allows` "Raj Nair" 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` "Raj Nair" DOES `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has gone into liquidation or has been dissolved` AT 30
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 377(2)(b) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within the further time the Registrar allows` "Raj Nair" 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` "Raj Nair" DOES `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has gone into liquidation or has been dissolved` AT 31
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 377(2)(b) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within the further time the Registrar allows` "Raj Nair" 30 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

-- the notice of the appointment of a liquidator: no time limit in the text, so with no event the duty stays open and a late act still fulfils it.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 377(2) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the appointment of a liquidator when one is appointed` "Raj Nair" 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 377(2) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the appointment of a liquidator when one is appointed` "Raj Nair" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` "Raj Nair" DOES `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator` AT 400

§ `Section 377(5) to (13): recording a dissolution, striking off, appeal`

-- (5)
#ASSERT `s 377(5) the Registrar must record in the register that the foreign company has been dissolved` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(5) the Registrar must record in the register that the foreign company has been dissolved` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (8) Arguments: satisfied of an unlawful purpose; of purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore; of use against the national security or interest.
#ASSERT `s 377(8) the Registrar must strike the name of the foreign company off the register` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(8) the Registrar must strike the name of the foreign company off the register` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(8) the Registrar must strike the name of the foreign company off the register` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(8) the Registrar must strike the name of the foreign company off the register` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (9)(b) Arguments: the day the sole authorised representative died; an authorised representative was appointed within 6 months; the day asked.
-- Died 1 January 2026: the 6 months run to 1 July 2026.
#ASSERT `s 377(9)(b) the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the death of its sole authorised representative` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(9)(b) the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the death of its sole authorised representative` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(9)(b) the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the death of its sole authorised representative` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (9) Arguments: reasonable cause to believe the company has ceased; the company has failed to appoint within 6 months.
#ASSERT `s 377(9) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(9) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(9) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if" without "only if": a Registrar with neither ground is not told by the text that he may not.
#ASSERT `s 377(9) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (10)(a) Arguments: written notice of the wish to resign given; notice under s 370(3) lodged; the day it was lodged; the company responded or appointed within 12 months; the day asked.
-- Lodged 1 March 2026: the 12 months run to 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(a) the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(a) the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(a) the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(a) the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(a) the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (10)(b) Arguments: a written request for instructions was sent; the day it was sent; the company gave instructions within 12 months; the day asked.
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(b) the foreign company has failed to give instructions within 12 months after the date the written request was sent` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(b) the foreign company has failed to give instructions within 12 months after the date the written request was sent` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(b) the foreign company has failed to give instructions within 12 months after the date the written request was sent` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(10)(b) the foreign company has failed to give instructions within 12 months after the date the written request was sent` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (10) Arguments: the sole authorised representative applied in the prescribed form; the Registrar is satisfied of paragraph (a); of paragraph (b).
#ASSERT `s 377(10) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register on the application of the sole authorised representative` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(10) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register on the application of the sole authorised representative` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no application: "upon the application of the sole authorised representative" (split site (ii): the text's own gate).
#ASSERT `s 377(10) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register on the application of the sole authorised representative` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an application, but the Registrar is not satisfied of either paragraph.
#ASSERT `s 377(10) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register on the application of the sole authorised representative` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (11), (12)
#ASSERT `s 377(11) the Registrar may have regard to the circumstances prescribed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(11) the Registrar may have regard to the circumstances prescribed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377(12) the provisions of this Act relating to the striking off of a defunct company apply with the adaptations necessary` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(12) the provisions of this Act relating to the striking off of a defunct company apply with the adaptations necessary` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (13) Arguments: the person is aggrieved; the decision is one under (8), (9) or (10); the day of the decision; the day the appeal is made. Decision 1 April 2026: the thirtieth day is 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 377(13) the person may appeal to the Minister` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(13) the person may appeal to the Minister` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 2 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377(13) the person may appeal to the Minister` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(13) the person may appeal to the Minister` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377(13) the person may appeal to the Minister` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377(13) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377(13) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 377A: application for administrative restoration`

-- (1) Arguments: the person is a director or member of the foreign company; its name has been struck off under section 377(9) or (10).
#ASSERT `s 377A(1) the person may apply to the Registrar to restore the name of the foreign company to the register` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377A(1) the person may apply to the Registrar to restore the name of the foreign company to the register` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377A(1) the person may apply to the Registrar to restore the name of the foreign company to the register` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) Arguments: the day the name was struck off; the day the application was received. Struck off 1 June 2026: the 6 years run to 1 June 2032.
-- "is not valid unless": received in time, the bar lifts and the text does not say valid; received late, the bar applies.
#ASSERT `s 377A(2) the application is not valid` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2032) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377A(2) the application is not valid` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2032) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377A(2) the application is not valid` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 377B: the Registrar's decision`

#ASSERT `s 377B(1) the Registrar must give notice to the applicant of the decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(1) the Registrar must give notice to the applicant of the decision` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) Arguments: the decision is to restore; the day the notice is sent.
#ASSERT `s 377B(2) the restoration date` TRUE (Date 5 5 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 5 2026)
#ASSERT `s 377B(2) the restoration date` FALSE (Date 5 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 377B(3)(a) the Registrar must enter in the register a note of the restoration date` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(3)(a) the Registrar must enter in the register a note of the restoration date` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377B(3)(b) the Registrar must cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(3)(b) the Registrar must cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4) Arguments: restored under a different name; the notice states the name; states the former name; states the unique entity number; states the restoration date.
#ASSERT `s 377B(4) the notice states everything the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(4) the notice states everything the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- restored under a different name: "that name and its former name".
#ASSERT `s 377B(4) the notice states everything the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377B(4) the notice states everything the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377B(4) the notice states everything the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377B(4) the notice states everything the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (5) Arguments: the decision is that the name should not be restored; the person made the application; the person is any other person aggrieved.
#ASSERT `s 377B(5) the person may appeal to the Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(5) the person may appeal to the Court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(5) the person may appeal to the Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377B(5) the person may appeal to the Court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6)
#ASSERT `s 377B(6)(a) the Court may confirm the Registrar's decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(6)(a) the Court may confirm the Registrar's decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377B(6)(b) the Court may restore the name of the foreign company to the register and give the directions and make the orders that section 377D(3) allows` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377B(6)(b) the Court may restore the name of the foreign company to the register and give the directions and make the orders that section 377D(3) allows` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 377C: restoration by the Registrar of a company struck off by mistake`

-- (2) a mistake made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by an applicant is excluded.
#ASSERT `s 377C(2) the mistake is a mistake of the Registrar within subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377C(2) the mistake is a mistake of the Registrar within subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377C(1) the Registrar may on his or her own initiative restore the name of the foreign company to the register` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377C(1) the Registrar may on his or her own initiative restore the name of the foreign company to the register` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: published in the Gazette; published on the Authority's website.
#ASSERT `s 377C(3) the Registrar may restore the name of the foreign company by publishing the notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377C(3) the Registrar may restore the name of the foreign company by publishing the notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377C(3) the Registrar may restore the name of the foreign company by publishing the notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377C(3) the day the restoration takes effect` TRUE (Date 9 9 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 9 2026)
#ASSERT `s 377C(3) the day the restoration takes effect` FALSE (Date 9 9 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 377D: effect of restoration`

-- (1) Arguments: restored under section 377B(2); restored under section 377C; restored on appeal under section 377B(5).
#ASSERT `s 377D(1) the foreign company is regarded as having continued its registration as if its name had not been struck off the register` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377D(1) the foreign company is regarded as having continued its registration as if its name had not been struck off the register` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377D(1) the foreign company is regarded as having continued its registration as if its name had not been struck off the register` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377D(1) the foreign company is regarded as having continued its registration as if its name had not been struck off the register` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) Arguments: the role of the person; the day struck off; the day the filing period ended; the day restored.
-- Struck off 1 January 2026, restored 1 December 2026: a filing period that ended on 1 June 2026 is between the two.
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: the foreign company` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the subsection names the company, its directors or equivalent persons, and authorised representatives; it says nothing of an officer or anyone else.
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: an officer of the foreign company` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: someone else` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the filing period must end "after" the striking off and "before" the restoration.
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: the foreign company` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: the foreign company` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: the foreign company` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` `s 365 role: the foreign company` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 377D(3) the Court may give directions and make orders as seem just for placing the foreign company and all other persons in the same position as if the name had not been struck off` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377D(3) the Court may give directions and make orders as seem just for placing the foreign company and all other persons in the same position as if the name had not been struck off` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4) Arguments: the day of restoration; the day the application to the Court is made. Restored 1 December 2026: the 3 years run to 1 December 2029.
#ASSERT `s 377D(4) the application to the Court for the directions or orders may be made` (Date 1 12 2026) (Date 1 12 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377D(4) the application to the Court for the directions or orders may be made` (Date 1 12 2026) (Date 2 12 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377D(4) the application to the Court for the directions or orders may be made` (Date 1 12 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
